# Drafted, not run: no host has loaded, enabled or started this unit (the worktree that authored it made no host
# changes). After adoption, stack-currency.timer starts it once a day. The template is not an installation
# claim; the inspected host's timer is not-found. It has no [Install] section, matching this directory's
# timer-triggered oneshot convention (codex-broker-reaper.service, host-requests-workstation.service). Why a timer
# and a due-file rather than a check at session start: docs/decisions/2026-09-30-session-currency-notice.md.
#
# @REPOSITORY@ is the checkout that holds scripts/currency_due.py. On the workstation that is the live clone,
# %h/code/native-agent-stack-live, as for credential-boot-receipt.service; never the working checkout, whose
# revision moves, and never a build worktree, which a merge deletes. Substitute it before installing, as for the
# other @REPOSITORY@ templates in this directory, and verify both units together (adoption/lifecycle.md):
#   sed 's#@REPOSITORY@#%h/code/native-agent-stack-live#g' adoption/templates/systemd/stack-currency.service > ~/.config/systemd/user/stack-currency.service
#   sed 's#@REPOSITORY@#%h/code/native-agent-stack-live#g' adoption/templates/systemd/upstream-surface-watch.service > ~/.config/systemd/user/upstream-surface-watch.service
#   cp adoption/templates/systemd/stack-currency.timer ~/.config/systemd/user/
#   systemd-analyze --user verify ~/.config/systemd/user/stack-currency.service ~/.config/systemd/user/upstream-surface-watch.service ~/.config/systemd/user/stack-currency.timer
#
# Wants= and After= run upstream-surface-watch.service (scripts/upstream_surface_watch.py --network) first, so that
# currency_due.py counts its fresh report; Wants= is weak, so a failed or missing watch unit never blocks this one
# (that unit's header quotes systemd.unit(5)). The separate ExecStartPre model proposal mode makes bounded,
# read-only primary-source checks; currency_due.py itself stays offline.
#
# The currency_due.py step makes no network call and writes nothing into the checkout. It runs
# receipt_staleness.py, adoption_status.py --pinned-versions, saturation_ledger.py --report and the offline
# active_model_currency.py check, then writes
# $XDG_STATE_HOME/native-agent-stack/currency-due.json (~/.local/state/... when XDG_STATE_HOME is unset; mode 0600)
# when something known is due, retaining earlier state on coverage gaps and removing it only after complete
# empty results. Known stale selectors return1; an incomplete model check is a gap, not a suppressed collection.
# Its --network option (runtime-worker skill pins through gh api)
# stays off here. A flag added to ExecStart changes the notice: the command that ends the due-file's summary_line
# repeats --network and a non-default --sweep-cadence-days, so it names the same flags as ExecStart (tests/
# test_currency_due.py checks that), and a skill check that cannot fetch leaves an earlier due-file in place.
#
# scripts/freshness_propose.py --model-currency reads catalogs/foundation/model-currency.json and checks each
# declared model/package line. HF metadata comes from the installed hf CLI with implicit credentials disabled;
# GitHub release checks use gh api --cache 120s and stop below 500 core requests remaining; PyPI uses its JSON API.
# Unknown sources remain unknown. Dated mode-0600 JSON/Markdown review proposals stay in private state under
# $XDG_STATE_HOME/native-agent-stack/model-currency (or ~/.local/state/...), including a landscape refresh from
# day five of its seven-day validity. It never applies a pin, downloads weights, changes models or publishes a PR.
# ExecStartPre's '-' keeps a malformed inventory or unavailable tool from suppressing the separate due-file.
#
# PATH: adoption_status.py --pinned-versions finds each version probe with shutil.which, and the user manager's own
# PATH lacks the ecosystem bin directory, so without this line every probe would be reported unchecked and
# pins_behind would read 0 (on the workstation on 2026-09-30 all six exec probes of the default profile resolved
# only there). On another host, use the directories that hold its pinned tools.
# PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 keeps this interpreter and the three it starts from writing __pycache__ into the
# checkout; -B on ExecStart would not reach the child interpreters.
# TimeoutStartSec= covers the script's own per-check bounds (120 s + 120 s + 600 s for the version probes); a
# oneshot has no start timeout by default (systemd.service(5)). UMask=0077 and NoNewPrivileges=true follow this
# directory's other oneshots.
[Unit]
Description=Propose model currency reviews and write the stack currency due-file (read-only checks)
Wants=upstream-surface-watch.service
After=upstream-surface-watch.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
UMask=0077
NoNewPrivileges=true
Nice=19
IOSchedulingClass=idle
TimeoutStartSec=900
Environment=PATH=%h/.local/share/codex-ecosystem/bin:%h/.local/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
Environment=PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1
ExecStartPre=-/usr/bin/python3 @REPOSITORY@/scripts/freshness_propose.py --model-currency
ExecStart=/usr/bin/python3 @REPOSITORY@/scripts/currency_due.py
